# Build artefacts at the repository ROOT only. These patterns must stay
# ANCHORED with a leading slash: unanchored, `weights.json` matches at every
# depth, which silently excluded snapshots/*/weights.json and
# snapshots/*/basket.json from version control. A snapshot exists to freeze
# the OUTPUT alongside the data and the parameters (tools/snapshot.py), so
# committing one without its weights file records a rebalance nobody can
# reconstruct — and it fails silently, which is the worst direction. Found
# 2026-08-18, before the first snapshot was ever committed.
/.cache/
.DS_Store
/weights.csv
/weights.json
/gate1_cap_weights.csv
/gate1_cap_weights.json
/basket.csv
/basket.json
/gate1_cap_basket.csv
/gate1_cap_basket.json
/market_bundle.json
/market_bars.csv
__pycache__/
/asymmetry.json
/asx_quotes.json

# Knowledge-base blobs. The registries (documents.jsonl, claims.jsonl,
# quarantine.jsonl, availability.jsonl) and the generated views ARE committed —
# they are the audit trail, and with them every content hash, every full
# retrieval URL and the channel it was reached through, which is what makes the
# bytes re-obtainable on another machine. The objects are ~1.3 GB of lodged PDFs
# and this repository has no LFS remote, so every document record carries
# `storage_state: "local"` and the audit reports the gap rather than pretending
# the store is portable. This arrangement is explicitly permitted by
# source-knowledge-base.md §6.4; promoting it to `durable` is a separate,
# reviewed decision.
/knowledge/objects/
/knowledge/extracted/
